  "id": "ddb51316892d_aHR0cHM6Ly9jYWxtdGFsa29uYm9hcmRpbmcuYmxvYi5jb3JlLndpbmRvd3MubmV0L2NhbG10YWxrYWRtaW5pdHJhdGlvbi9DYWxtJTIwVGFsayUyME9uYm9hcmRpbmclMjBHdWlkZS5wZGY1_markdown_document_0",
  "content": "To maintain clinical standards and regulatory compliance, therapists must submit valid copies of\r\nthe following documents during registration:\r\n\r\n. Government-Issued Photo ID: Valid Passport, Driver\u0027s License, or National Identification\r\nCard.\r\n\r\n\u00B7 Professional License: Active mental health license (e.g., Licensed Clinical Psychologist,\r\nLMFT, LCSW, LPC) issued by the relevant state or national regulatory authority.\r\n\r\n\u00B7 Academic Credentials: Master\u0027s or Doctoral degree certificate in psychology, counseling,\r\nsocial work, or a related mental health field.\r\n\r\n\u00B7 Proof of Malpractice Insurance: Current professional liability/malpractice insurance policy\r\ncertificate meeting minimum coverage requirements.\r\n\r\n\u00B7 Updated Curriculum Vitae (CV): Documenting clinical experience, specialties, and\r\nprofessional background.\r\n\r\n\u00B7 Direct Deposit / Banking Information: Voided check, official bank statement header, or\r\nverified bank document containing account holder name, IBAN/Account Number, and\r\nSWIFT/Routing code.",
